        {
          "kicker": "National contracts",
          "heading": "Steve Borthwick seeks national team progress from £264m Premiership club agreement",
          "body": "Two years after the Rugby Football Union signed a £264m Professional Game Partnership with Premiership clubs, Steve Borthwick's England side has yet to see the expected benefits on the international stage. With the next World Cup only 12 months away, questions remain over the national team's progress under the deal. Although the agreement allows Borthwick to award 25 enhanced player contracts to gain greater squad control, the actual level of influence remains highly debated while domestic clubs continue to prioritise their own commercial recovery."
        },
