          "heading": "Deian Gwynne named potential World Cup bolter amid difficult Wales season forecast",
          "body": "Gloucester back-rower Deian Gwynne has been identified as a surprise contender for the senior squad ahead of next year’s World Cup. The former Wales U20 captain, currently playing in the Gallagher Premiership, is viewed as a potential bolter for Steve Tandy’s side during a season that includes the upcoming Nations Championship. Forecasts suggest Wales face a battle to avoid a fourth successive Six Nations wooden spoon following recent heavy defeats to Argentina and South Africa on the summer tour."
